{{- /* sitemap.xml — the per-language <urlset>.

       Hugo builds this file from its own embedded template, which lists every
       page in the language. This overrides it to do two things more.

       One: drop the pages [params.aeo] disallow excludes. A sitemap is an
       invitation to fetch a URL. Listing one that robots.txt blocks on the same
       host is the two files disagreeing in the direction that costs something —
       Google Search Console reports it as "Submitted URL blocked by
       robots.txt", and the whole point of the key is that a path excluded from
       crawling is excluded everywhere the site describes itself. llms.txt,
       llms-full.txt and the markdown twins already honour it; this was the one
       published file that did not.

       Two: host aeo-selfcheck.html's deferred half. That check has to run from
       a template that renders no matter how the site is configured, and this is
       the only one the module ships that does — robots.txt needs
       enableRobotsTXT, llms.txt needs [outputs], and the head partials need the
       theme to call them. It also has to run from a template that is not HTML:
       a page carrying a templates.Defer block is not minified the same way, and
       the placeholder left one byte of whitespace in every consumer's home page
       — measured against a real theme, where the migration was otherwise
       byte-identical. An XML file the module writes itself is a place where
       that cost is visible and controlled, and here it is zero.

       On a single-language site this is the file at /sitemap.xml, and it is the
       only place the exclusion can happen — sitemapindex.xml is never rendered
       there at all. On a multilingual site it is each language's sub-sitemap,
       and the flat option in sitemapindex.xml filters its own copy the same way.

       Everything below the two partial calls is Hugo's embedded sitemap.xml,
       kept faithful to v0.163 down to the whitespace — `</url><url>` between
       entries and all — and written to be diffed against the upstream file
       rather than tidied. Overriding a built-in *replaces* it, so this has to
       reproduce it rather than fall through to it. That is the maintenance cost
       of the override, and it is the same one sitemapindex.xml already carries.
       Matching byte for byte is what lets a site adopting this module diff its
       output and see nothing move.

       Context: the sitemap page. `.Pages` here is the language's own, so
       aeo-allowed.html's default root — this language's home — is the right
       one, and no override is needed. */ -}}
{{- $aeo := partialCached "aeo-params-table.html" (dict "value" site.Params.aeo "path" "[params.aeo]") "aeo" site.Language.Lang -}}
{{- $disallow := partialCached "aeo-params-list.html" (dict "value" $aeo.disallow "path" "[params.aeo] disallow" "maps" false) "aeo.disallow" site.Language.Lang -}}
{{- partial "aeo-selfcheck-robots.html" . -}}
{{ printf "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?>" | safeHTML }}
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9"
  xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
  {{ range partial "aeo-allowed.html" (dict "pages" (where .Pages "Sitemap.Disable" "ne" true) "disallow" $disallow) }}{{ if .Permalink }}<url>
    <loc>{{ .Permalink }}</loc>{{ if not .Lastmod.IsZero }}
    <lastmod>{{ safeHTML ( .Lastmod.Format "2006-01-02T15:04:05-07:00" ) }}</lastmod>{{ end }}{{ with .Sitemap.ChangeFreq }}
    <changefreq>{{ . }}</changefreq>{{ end }}{{ if ge .Sitemap.Priority 0.0 }}
    <priority>{{ .Sitemap.Priority }}</priority>{{ end }}{{ if .IsTranslated }}{{ range .AllTranslations }}
    <xhtml:link
                rel="alternate"
                hreflang="{{ .Language.Locale }}"
                href="{{ .Permalink }}"
                />{{ end }}{{ end }}
  </url>{{ end }}{{ end }}
</urlset>
